# lobby-connect-idle — real capture (WBS-3.1.1.4)
#
# `mock-client run` against the FAF test lobby, authenticating as the seeded
# `test` account (id 7982) and going idle. Captured 2026-07-14, on the final
# integrated code path: run drives the lifecycle FSM (WBS-3.1.3.1) via
# LobbySession, authenticating through the refresh-token file channel.
#
# Endpoint:  wss://ws.faforever.xyz   (the working test endpoint — lobby-protocol-spec.md "Server Endpoints")
# unique_id: generated at runtime by the FAF `faf-uid` binary (--uid-binary-path); the
#            lobby's policy server rejects a placeholder UID. See README "run".
# Command:   mock-client run --config mock-client.json --uid-binary-path <faf-uid>
#
# Console format (the same events are written as structured JSON to logs/<component>.jsonl).
# No credentials appear: the access token, refresh token, and the faf-uid blob are never
# logged — only the blob's length and the server-supplied login/id. The refresh token was
# rotated and persisted back to the token file by the run (verified via file mtime).

