# After ~20s idle (transport auto-ponging lobby pings), SIGTERM triggered the shutdown
# hook: the WebSocket close frame is sent cleanly and the process exits 143 (the JVM
# default for SIGTERM — see README "Exit codes"). The hook's own log line and the server's
# close echo can arrive after the JVM has already halted, so those final lines are not
# always flushed; no error lines at shutdown.
#
# The WARN lines are expected: 'notice', 'irc_password', 'player_info', 'social', and
# 'game_info' are lobby broadcasts with no registered handler yet — they belong to later
# stories (matchmaking 3.1.1.x, game_info consumption). Each is logged once then muted.
#
# This capture used `timeout --signal=TERM 20` as a stand-in for an interactive Ctrl-C.
